### Changed

- Integrate the M9 Frontend Redesign into `main` and add the v1.9.0 release notes. ([#244](https://github.com/goldbarth/ServiceDeskLite/pull/244))

### Added

- Add inline citation badges to sanitized assistant Markdown answers, with numbered sources and hover or focus tooltips. ([#245](https://github.com/goldbarth/ServiceDeskLite/pull/245))
- Make the first actionable `SuggestedNextSteps` item a ticket-header control that performs its mapped action, with remaining steps in an overflow menu. ([#237](https://github.com/goldbarth/ServiceDeskLite/pull/237))
- Add a keyboard-operated command palette to `MainLayout`, with navigation targets from `NavRegistry` and debounced, cancellable ticket search. ([#236](https://github.com/goldbarth/ServiceDeskLite/pull/236))
- Update ticket status optimistically on the board and detail view, then reconcile successful changes or restore the prior state on rejection. ([#235](https://github.com/goldbarth/ServiceDeskLite/pull/235))
- Replace the ticket detail status and assignee dialogs with inline `MudMenu` popovers that use the existing command handlers. ([#234](https://github.com/goldbarth/ServiceDeskLite/pull/234))
- Anchor assistant citations to matching titles in answer text with numbered badges and hover or keyboard-focus tooltips, retaining a sources list for unanchored citations. ([#233](https://github.com/goldbarth/ServiceDeskLite/pull/233))
- Add the active agent roster to each chat system prompt and direct the assistant to use only listed names when assigning tickets. ([#221](https://github.com/goldbarth/ServiceDeskLite/pull/221))
- Require `AgentLoop` to call `check_grounding` once after retrieval when no grounding check has run. ([#218](https://github.com/goldbarth/ServiceDeskLite/pull/218))
- Centralize frontend palette, spacing, radius, elevation, and semantic chip colors in design tokens, and use `KpiAccent` to identify tones in `KpiCard`. ([#213](https://github.com/goldbarth/ServiceDeskLite/pull/213))

### Fixed

- Wrap the board-card title link so its two-line clamp works without grid-item blockification. ([#240](https://github.com/goldbarth/ServiceDeskLite/pull/240))
- Apply the assistant panel styles through `::deep .assistant-chat` so the composer stays inset within the panel. ([#239](https://github.com/goldbarth/ServiceDeskLite/pull/239))
- Set the `Category` column width to `140px` and render its header with the uppercase `tickets-table__label` class. ([#238](https://github.com/goldbarth/ServiceDeskLite/pull/238))
- Add chat system-prompt rules requiring successful tool results before claiming a change and avoiding confirmation when the user has already requested an action. ([#223](https://github.com/goldbarth/ServiceDeskLite/pull/223))
- Convert ticket summary timestamps to the user timezone from `Anthropic:UserTimeZone` before including them in the model prompt. ([#222](https://github.com/goldbarth/ServiceDeskLite/pull/222))
- Return `IsError: true` for failed knowledge-base searches while preserving the distinct unavailable result and transient-fault retry behavior. ([#220](https://github.com/goldbarth/ServiceDeskLite/pull/220))
- Score grounding with `SemanticGroundingEvaluator` using cosine similarity to retrieved passages, falling back to `LexicalGroundingEvaluator` when embeddings are unavailable or fail. ([#219](https://github.com/goldbarth/ServiceDeskLite/pull/219))
